⭐ COMPLETE SPRING MVC REQUEST FLOW (BEGINNER FRIENDLY)
This is the flow:

Browser → DispatcherServlet → HandlerMapping → Controller → Service → Model → ViewResolver → HTML Page
Let's break this down with your real example:

✅ STEP 1 — User sends request from browser
User opens:

http://localhost:8080/
This request reaches embedded Tomcat, which is inside Spring Boot.

✅ STEP 2 — DispatcherServlet receives the request
Spring Boot automatically creates:

DispatcherServlet
This is the Front Controller in Spring MVC.

📌 It handles ALL requests.
📌 It decides which controller must handle this URL.

So:

/  → goes to DispatcherServlet
✅ STEP 3 — DispatcherServlet asks HandlerMapping
DispatcherServlet asks:

"Which controller method should handle this URL?"

Spring uses Handler Mapping to find:

@GetMapping("/")
public String home(Model model)
So it says:

✔ Correct handler found → HomeController.home()

✅ STEP 4 — Spring calls Controller Method
Spring now calls your controller:

@GetMapping("/")
public String home(Model model) {
    model.addAttribute("message", "Welcome to Student Web App!");
    return "home";
}
What happens here?

You add data into Model

You return string "home"

🧠 IMPORTANT:
Returning "home" does NOT mean return “home string”.
It means:

“Find and render home.html from templates folder.”

✅ STEP 5 — Controller returns View Name (“home”)
Controller returns:

"home"
DispatcherServlet receives this and says:

"Now I need to find a page called home.html"

✅ STEP 6 — ViewResolver resolves the HTML file
Spring Boot automatically configures ThymeleafViewResolver.

It maps:

"home"  →  src/main/resources/templates/home.html
✔ It loads the HTML
✔ It replaces dynamic data (using Thymeleaf)

Example:

<h1 th:text="${message}"></h1>
message = "Welcome to Student Web App!"
So final output becomes:

<h1>Welcome to Student Web App!</h1>
✅ STEP 7 — HTML page sent to browser
DispatcherServlet returns the final rendered HTML.

Browser displays:

Welcome to Student Web App!
✔ FLOW SUMMARY (in simple words)
1. User hits URL
http://localhost:8080/students
2. DispatcherServlet catches it
3. HandlerMapping finds controller method
@GetMapping("/students")
4. Controller fetches data
From service:

service.getStudents()
5. Add data to Model
model.addAttribute("students", students);
6. Return view name
return "students";
7. Thymeleaf finds templates/students.html
8. Page rendered and shown to browser
